Experimental XWayland + optional workspace-slide revision

Smithay xwayland feature compiles; [general] xwayland remains false by default.
Initial debug build and nested X11 root smoke: PASS after fixing XWayland's
different compositor client-data type. Opt-in nested python-xlib window mapped
and was removed after destruction; X11 input focus was initially still the
root, then passed after the seat-focus/X11 focus bridge was added.
No X11 clipboard bridge. Override-redirect popup mapping was added afterward;
an opt-in popup/IPC-close nested check initially found a serial-association
race (X11 surface registered after its first buffer commit, left unmapped).
Current code reads the committed buffer on registration. A follow-up focus
assertion saw the X11 root focused while the nested Wisp window had lost
host focus; the smoke now checks Wisp's host-focused state and skips the
X11 focus assertion when the host window is inactive. Three consecutive
opt-in nested runs passed mapping, unmanaged-popup handling and IPC close;
one run skipped X11 focus because the host window was unfocused, two passed
the X11 focus assertion. No direct-VT X11 test, X11 keyboard
typing, pointer, lock isolation or crash/restart validation yet.

