in foot returning the X11 text. Both clipboard directions passed with real
xterm/foot clients. The xterm legacy-font warning appeared on an earlier
invocation; the screenshot shows a running xterm. Primary selection and
xterm-visible lock isolation have not yet been reported by the user.

User follow-up: primary selection works in the nested foot/xterm test. With
xterm open, swaylock launched from foot hid everything including xterm; after
unlock, the user reported that everything returned to normal. This is a
user-observed nested check, not a measured security guarantee or direct-VT
